, since the incident, Koyomi seems to meet girls who have an apparition-related issue. Hitagi Senjougahara doesn’t weigh anything, Suruga Kanbaru’s right arm becomes like that of a monkey’s, and a young girl, Mayoi, cannot find her way home no matter how many times she tries. Koyomi, a Mr. Nice Guy, ends up helping each and every girl solve her problem with the help of Meme Oshino.\n\n(Source: Aniplex)\n\nNote: Only the first 12 episodes were broadcast on television; the remaining three episodes were distributed on the anime's website between November 3, 2009, and June 25, 2010."},"tags":[{"name":"Youkai","rank":93,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Urban Fantasy","rank":91,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Ensemble Cast","rank":91,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Surreal Comedy","rank":89,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":87,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Philosophy","rank":84,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Kuudere","rank":82,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Coming of Age","rank":81,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Vampire","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Female Cast","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Ghost","rank":79,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Satire","rank":77,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Heterosexual","rank":76,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Teen Cast","rank":76,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Meta","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Dissociative Identities","rank":74,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Psychosexual","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Curses","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Monster Girl","rank":68,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Mixed Media","rank":66,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Unrequited Love","rank":66,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Parody","rank":65,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gore","rank":65,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Exorcism","rank":65,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Rotoscoping","rank":64,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gods","rank":64,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Love Triangle","rank":63,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Yandere","rank":61,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Tomboy","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"n